16
00:00:32.287 --> 00:00:33.087
her.

17
00:00:33.404 --> 00:00:35.824
So she carried a spare sari.

18
00:00:35.824 --> 00:00:38.184
At school, she changed, and

19
00:00:38.184 --> 00:00:39.694
began the lesson.

20
00:00:40.287 --> 00:00:41.900
By the end of eighteen fifty

21
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.507
one, the Phules ran three girls'

22
00:00:44.507 --> 00:00:45.587
schools in Pune.

23
00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:48.227
Her friend Fatima Sheikh taught

24
00:00:48.227 --> 00:00:49.697
alongside her.

25
00:00:50.119 --> 00:00:52.299
In eighteen fifty two, the

26
00:00:52.299 --> 00:00:54.139
British government declared her

27
00:00:54.139 --> 00:00:56.239
the best teacher in the state.

28
00:00:56.239 --> 00:00:58.219
Her critics on the road were

29
00:00:58.219 --> 00:00:59.689
slower to agree.

30
00:01:00.261 --> 00:01:02.361
In eighteen fifty four came her

31
00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:04.561
first book of poems, Kavya

32
00:01:04.561 --> 00:01:07.201
Phule. One of her poems has a

33
00:01:07.201 --> 00:01:08.941
title that says it all:

34
00:01:08.941 --> 00:01:11.151
"Go, get education."

35
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.820
For GS1 and the Essay:

36
00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.880
Savitribai Phule, a pioneer of

37
00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:17.560
girls' education.

38
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.960
With Jyotirao, she opened

39
00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.040
schools for girls in Pune from

40
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.896
eighteen forty eight.

41
00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:26.869
Two saris.

42
00:01:26.869 --> 00:01:28.369
One long walk.

43
00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:30.509
And every morning, she went

44
00:01:30.509 --> 00:01:31.309
again.
